From 9e178268362f997a5484c48d27b5cc44f3e7ab9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@inscope-labs.dev>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 01:44:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shell): Phase 2.6 - rewrite BinaryRegistry/TierManifest
 for real manifest schema

BinaryRegistry.kt and its TierManifest/BinaryDescriptor model were still
written against the old obsolete draft schema (per-binary nativeLibName +
fallbackSystemPath, no sharedBinaries, no hash verification) -- it never
matched what base.json/standard.json actually ship since bf0df46/8e4e50b.

- TierManifest now carries an optional source block (project/license/
  upstreamVersion/mirrorUrl/commit) and a sharedBinaries[] list, matching
  base.json/standard.json exactly.
- BinaryDescriptor drops nativeLibName/fallbackSystemPath (those never
  belonged per-applet) in favor of a sharedBinary id reference, resolved
  against the owning tier's sharedBinaries[] at lookup time.
- resolveBinaryPath() now verifies the resolved file's SHA-256 against
  the manifest hash for the device's primary supported ABI before
  returning a path -- a corrupted or tampered .so no longer silently
  executes. Verification result is cached per nativeLibName so repeat
  command invocations don't re-hash the same binary every call.
- Updated the one UI caller (LocalShellModulesSheet) that referenced the
  removed tier-level "description" field to build a label from
  source.project + source.upstreamVersion instead.
- Rewrote TierManifestTest.kt against the real schema; added a
  resolveBinaryPath fail-closed test for an unknown binary name.

Known follow-up: extended.json on disk is still the old obsolete draft
(per-binary nativeLibName, no sharedBinary refs) -- it will now fail to
parse under the new schema (caught, logged, EXTENDED manifest loads as
null) until it's replaced the same way standard.json was. Expected,
since Extended's real manifest work starts next with sqlite3.

Not compiled/tested against a real Android toolchain in this sandbox --
needs a build pass (AI Studio / Android Studio) before merge.
